author ai
group gui
note The file viewer, and the one place a human can author a step. Only the rows on screen become elements - a spacer stands in for everything above and below - which is what makes a four-thousand-line file scroll at the same cost as a short one. Each row is numbered, syntax coloured, and carries a coloured bar on the left where a step of the selected path is anchored, green when current and red when stale. Clicking selects a line and shift-clicking extends the selection, which the top bar's 'pin selection' then turns into a step; double-clicking or ctrl-clicking an identifier jumps to its definition instead, and alt-clicking pins it in the peek panel.

